# Scripts and unit files that execute on Linux targets (routers, servers) must
# stay LF in the working tree even on Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true:
# busybox ash, procd and systemd cannot parse CRLF. These files also ship inside
# release tarballs built from a checkout (make package-openwrt normalizes too).
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.init    text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf
